lesson: 195
title: Metres and centimetres in several steps
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One metre is 100 centimetres. Turn a length like 3 m 45 cm into centimetres first: 3 × 100 + 45 = 345 cm.
explain: Then work in centimetres: cutting 4 pieces of 60 cm takes 4 × 60 = 240 cm, so 345 - 240 = 105 cm are left.
vars: a=name L=2..9 c1=5..95 k=2..6 c2=15..90 w=2..5
let: total = 100 * L + c1
need: total - k * c2 >= 5
answer: total - k * c2
exercise: A rope is {L} m {c1} cm long. {a} cuts off {k} pieces, each {c2} cm long. How many centimetres of rope are left?
exercise: {a} has a ribbon {L} m {c1} cm long and uses {c2} cm of it for each of {k} gift boxes. How many centimetres of ribbon remain?
exercise: {k} shelves, each {c2} cm long, are sawn from a board {L} m {c1} cm long. How many centimetres of the board are left?
exercise: A roll of tape is {L} m {c1} cm long. {a} uses {k} strips of {c2} cm. How many centimetres of tape are still on the roll?
exercise: A wire {L} m {c1} cm long is cut into {k} pieces of {c2} cm, and what is left makes one last piece. How long is the last piece in centimetres?
test: How many centimetres are left of a piece of cloth {L} m {c1} cm long after {a} cuts {k} strips of {c2} cm from it?
test: {a} hops {c2} cm with every hop. After {k} hops, how many centimetres is {a.he} from a line that was {L} m {c1} cm ahead of {a.him}?
test: A fence is {L} m {c1} cm long. {a} has painted {k} parts of it, each {c2} cm long. How many centimetres of the fence are not yet painted?
test: The ribbon is {L} m {c1} cm long and {w} cm wide. After {k} bows using {c2} cm each are tied from it, how many centimetres of its length are left?
exercise: {a} has {L} m {c1} cm of rope and cuts {k} pieces of {c2} cm from it. How many centimetres of rope remain?
exercise: How many centimetres of ribbon are left when {k} pieces of {c2} cm each are cut from a ribbon {L} m {c1} cm long?
exercise: A carpenter in Vermont saws {k} pieces of {c2} cm each from a plank {L} m {c1} cm long. How much of the plank, in centimetres, is still left?
exercise: A rope of {L} m {c1} cm; {k} pieces of {c2} cm cut off. How many centimetres are left?
exercise: {a} uses {c2} cm of string for each of {k} kites. The string was {L} m {c1} cm long. How many centimetres of string does {a.he} still have?
exercise: A tailor in London has {L} m {c1} cm of cloth and cuts {k} strips, every strip {c2} cm long. How many centimetres of cloth are left over?
exercise: From a hose {L} m {c1} cm long, {a} cuts {k} pieces of {c2.words} centimetres. How many centimetres of hose remain?
exercise: {a} in Melbourne has a strip of garden edging {L} m {c1} cm long. {a.He} cuts off {k} lengths of {c2} cm. How many centimetres of the strip remain?
test: What length, in centimetres, is left of a cable {L} m {c1} cm long once {k} bits of {c2} cm each have been cut off?
test: A path in a park in Ontario is {L} m {c1} cm long. {a} has swept {k} sections of it, each {c2} cm long. How many centimetres are still to be swept?
test: {a} takes {k} steps along a hall {L} m {c1} cm long, and each step is {c2} cm. How many centimetres of the hall are still in front of {a.him}?
test: After {k} pieces of {c2} cm are taken from a roll of wrapping paper {L} m {c1} cm long, what length of paper is left on the roll, in centimetres?
test: A shelf in a classroom in Dublin is {L} m {c1} cm long. {k} boxes, each {c2} cm wide, stand on it side by side. How many centimetres of the shelf are empty?
test: A ribbon is {L} m {c1} cm long and costs {w} dollars. {a} cuts {k} pieces of {c2} cm from it. How many centimetres of ribbon are left?
exercise: rope {L} m {c1} cm, {a} cuts {k} bits {c2} cm each. how many cm left
exercise: ribbon {L} m {c1} cm, {c2} cm for each of {k+1} — no hang on, {k} presents. cm left?
exercise: cloth {L} m {c1} cm, {a} cuts {k} strips {c2} cm each, took {w} goes to find the scissors lol. how many cm left
exercise: {a} says {L*100+c1-c2} cm left. nah {a.he} cut {k} of em. {L} m {c1} cm of string, {k} pieces of {c2} cm off. left in cm?
test: how many cm of tape left, {L} m {c1} cm roll, cut {k} strips {c2} cm
test: {L} m {c1+1} cm, no sorry {L} m {c1} cm of wire, {k} bits {c2} cm cut off, rest in cm?
test: {a} thinks {L} m {c1} cm is {10*L+c1} cm lol. cut {k} bits of {c2} cm off it, how many cm left really
exam: A rope measures {L} metres {c1} centimetres in length. Whereas {k} pieces, each of {c2} centimetres, are removed from it, determine the length of rope remaining, expressed in centimetres.
exam: It is given that {a} possesses a ribbon of {L} m {c1} cm and employs {c2} cm thereof in respect of each of {k} parcels. Ascertain the remaining length in centimetres.
exam: State, in centimetres, the length which remains of a cable of {L} metres and {c1} centimetres subsequent to the removal of {k} lengths of {c2} centimetres each.
exam: Compute the residual length, in centimetres, of a roll of tape measuring {L} m {c1} cm, given that {k} strips of {c2} cm each have been cut therefrom.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} a rope {L} m {c1} cm long. {a} cuts off {k} pieces of {c2} cm each for skipping ropes. How many centimetres of rope are left?
exercise: {a}'s brother was economical with the truth: he said he cut only one piece off the {L} m {c1} cm ribbon. Really he cut off {k} pieces of {c2} cm each. How many centimetres of ribbon are left?
test: the cat had a 'little accident' on the rope, gross, so we cut {k} bits of {c2} cm off. rope was {L} m {c1} cm. how many cm left
